[38;5;252m[1m## Two UB sites I verified rather than trusted[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust source contains comments asserting things about C's undefined behavior. Both needed checking, since a wrong guess there is invisible to ordinary testing.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mNegative index into [38;5;10m"+*-%"[0m.[22m For [38;5;10mtree_sum < 0[0m, C's truncating [38;5;10m%[0m yields index −1…−3, reading [3mbefore[23m the literal. The Rust translation substitutes [38;5;10m0[0m and relies on [38;5;10mparse_operation[0m falling through to [38;5;10mOP_ADD[0m. In [38;5;10m.rodata[0m the literal sits at [38;5;10m0x2032[0m, directly after [38;5;10m"left-left\0"[0m, so those bytes are [38;5;10m0x00[0m, [38;5;10m't'[0m, [38;5;10m'f'[0m — none an operator character, so C does reach [38;5;10mOP_ADD[0m. The assumption holds, but it is layout-dependent, so I rebuilt the C library with gcc [38;5;10m-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os[0m and clang [38;5;10m-O0/-O2[0m and re-ran the whole suite against each ([38;5;10mC_SO_PATH=… cargo test[0m). All 7 variants pass. [38;5;10minreftree_covers_every_residue_positive_and_negative[0m drives sums from −60 to 60 to hit every residue.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m[38;5;10mINT_MIN / -1[0m.[22m [38;5;10mdivide_op[0m/[38;5;10mmodulo_op[0m use [38;5;10mwrapping_div[0m/[38;5;10mwrapping_rem[0m, but on x86 [38;5;10midiv[0m traps: C raises SIGFPE where Rust returns a value. This input pair is explicitly excluded from the sweep with a comment, since a signal has no comparable return value. It is unreachable from [38;5;10minreftree[0m (the operator is never [38;5;10m/[0m, and the divisor is always 1 or 2).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Coverage notes[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Level 2 compares the raw bytes of the entire 50-entry [38;5;10mnode_table[0m plus [38;5;10mnode_count[0m after every single call, which catches behavior the return value hides — notably that a bad [38;5;10mparent_id[0m returns −1 [3mafter[23m already writing the node into [38;5;10mnode_table[node_count][0m, and that [38;5;10mstrncpy[0m's zero-padding wipes stale bytes (tested against a table pre-filled with [38;5;10m0xAB[0m).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10minreftree[0m is checked over an exhaustive 9⁴ grid, extreme values, 8000 pseudorandom cases, and against a hand-derived model of the C semantics — the model check matters because it distinguishes "both agree" from "both wrong in the same way".[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two harness issues surfaced along the way, both mine rather than the translation's: tests initially ran in parallel against one shared copy of the globals (one test setting [38;5;10mnode_count = INT_MAX[0m segfaulted another mid-scan), fixed with a process-wide mutex; and one test asserted a full table using parent id [38;5;10m0[0m, which never exists, so those inserts were correctly rejected.[0m[0m
